SUMMARY:Lost & Found: An Immersive Open-World Puzzle Adventure
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a real 1800s village transformed into Canada’s largest immersive open-world puzzle adventure. \nLost & Found invites you to explore 30 acres and 43 historic buildings at The Village at Black Creek. Choose your own quests\, interact with live characters\, solve immersive puzzles\, and uncover a hidden treasure that could save the town. \nUnlike traditional escape rooms\, this is a fully self-guided experience; no timers\, no fixed path. Your team decides where to go and which mysteries to pursue. \nWhat to Expect: \n\nUp to 4 hours of gameplay\n20+ interactive quests\n10 story-driven characters\nDesigned for teams of 2-4\nMultiple visits encouraged\n\nStory:The creek has run dry. The mill stands abandoned. If you can earn the villagers’ trust and locate the hidden treasure\, Black Creek may have a chance at survival. \nRunning: June – November 2026 on Saturdays and Sundays from 11AM – 4PM \nTickets: \n\nGeneral Admission: $48 + HST \nChild (4-14): $28 + HST \nChildren 3 and under: Free\n\nAdvance booking recommended. \nLearn more at secretcityadventures.com/lost-and-found
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/lost-found-an-immersive-open-world-puzzle-adventure/
LOCATION:The Village at Black Creek\, 1000 Murray Ross Pkwy\, North York\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M3J 2P3
CATEGORIES:Comedy & Improv,Games & Trivia,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/lost-found-an-immersive-open-world-puzzle-adventure.jpg
END:VEVENT
