SUMMARY:You'll See
DESCRIPTION:Ulysses for children? Yes\, Ulysses for children. \nJames Joyce’s epic story of one day in one city is brought to life in this inventive new show\, bringing Ireland’s most notorious book to audiences aged 8 and upwards\, and to all those who haven’t got around to reading it yet. \nCombining live performance\, intricate paper design\, an original score and Joyce’s odyssey\, this is theatre that will excite both young and old. \n“Ulysses for children: has the world gone mad?… Branar has gone and done it.” ★★★★— The Irish Times \n“Never read Ulysses? No worries at all. Branar brings the bones of James Joyce’s epic novel to life with charm and fun. A captivating adaptation devised for children but enthralling for everyone.”— Fringe Review UK \nThis play is part of the Canada Ireland Foundation’s Bealtaine Theatre Festival\, which brings the best of Irish Theatre to Toronto. An annual celebration\, the Bealtaine Theatre Festival features Canadian premieres of some of Ireland’s most captivating and contemporary theatre. Bealtaine will be held May 21 to June 7 at the Corleck — a brand new performance venue on Toronto’s waterfront. Learn more. \nYOU’LL SEEby BranarAdapted by Marc Mac Lochlainn and Helen GreggDirected by Marc Mac LochlainnFeaturing Helen Gregg \nRecommended for Ages 8+
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/youll-see/
LOCATION:The Corleck Building\, 3 Eireann Quay\, Toronto\, ON M5V 0A3\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5V 0A3
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/youll-see-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
